# GRADUATED — green on Rust `gg` (both backends) AND on the self-host lane.
#
# History: this cell was `gg check`-clean and exited 139 on both real backends.
# It was ONE of `todo/t0406`'s six repro cells (non-identifier-callee /
# signature-erased container element). The Rust lane graduated it with the
# dispatch-name + `clone_fn_for_ptr` arms; the self-host lane followed when the
# generic-call-vs-index parse stopped DELETING the `[0]` and the `ECall` callee
# dispatcher stopped discarding a non-identifier callee. `todo/t0406` stays open
# on its four `&`-sigil cells.
#
# The full callee-shape axis lives in `callable_callee_shape_axis.gg`; this
# fixture stays as the no-sigil `Vector`-element cell it was filed as.
#
# What this cell DISCRIMINATES from that item's remaining repros:
# they all carry a `&` sigil, so their story is "the borrow tag never reaches
# either ABI channel". This one has NO sigil at all — a pure by-value
# `Callable[int(int)]` — and it dies just the same, which shows the defect is
# the element signature collapsing to the zero-parameter fallback
# `fn() -> i64`, not the sigil tagging.
#
# `push` + `len()` on the same vector was GREEN throughout (the closure-packing
# wrap at `AbiKind::VoidElem` handles the write); only calling the element back
# out died, on BOTH read shapes below.
#
# DISCRIMINATED from todo/t0873, the other open `Vector[Callable]` item: that
# one is a container-LITERAL SEGV and a NULL `elem_drop` (the pushed envs leak).
# This cell pushes, so it is past the literal arm, and it died on the CALL, not
# at drop.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the wired test): prints `1` then `42` then `42`.

void main():
    Callable[int(int)] f = (int x): x * 2
    Vector[Callable[int(int)]] fs = []
    fs.push(f.clone())
    print(f"{fs.len()}")
    # index-read call
    print(f"{fs[0](21)}")
    # get-chain call through a bound local
    Callable[int(int)] g = fs.get(0).unwrap()
    print(f"{g(21)}")
